WEBVTT

00:05.820 --> 00:06.780
Hey!

00:06.780 --> 00:08.200
Wait a minute!

00:12.740 --> 00:15.250
What was that just now?

00:15.910 --> 00:18.040
Why were Inukami-senpai and Kazuki dead?!

00:19.360 --> 00:20.920
I have to ask her!

00:25.800 --> 00:26.770
I'm begging you...

00:27.170 --> 00:28.680
Only you can change the future.

00:45.570 --> 00:50.240
THE WRONG WAY TO USE HEALING MAGIC

02:00.980 --> 02:01.860
#7 THE NIGHT OF RESOLVE!

02:01.860 --> 02:03.810
#7 THE NIGHT OF RESOLVE!
A fox beastman girl?

02:03.810 --> 02:05.520
#7 THE NIGHT OF RESOLVE!
No, I haven't seen her come this way.

02:05.860 --> 02:07.610
I guess not.

02:07.610 --> 02:09.650
She was still young...

02:09.650 --> 02:12.150
she couldn't have gotten far.

02:12.150 --> 02:15.700
Damn it!
Where did that little fox go?

02:15.700 --> 02:17.990
What's with all the commotion?

02:19.180 --> 02:20.200
Captain?

02:20.560 --> 02:23.000
I-I'll head back to my post!

02:23.000 --> 02:24.210
Don't mind me!

02:25.170 --> 02:26.390
Thomas-san...

02:26.390 --> 02:29.550
He's still scared of you, huh?

02:29.550 --> 02:32.470
Not like I can't understand him.

02:34.260 --> 02:36.800
Ouch! Ouch! Ow, ow, ow!

02:36.800 --> 02:38.180
Just what do you understand?

02:38.180 --> 02:39.260
Come again?

02:39.260 --> 02:42.100
Stop! Nothing! Nothing at all!

02:42.850 --> 02:44.850
Where have you been, anyway?

02:45.980 --> 02:48.020
Just a short trip to the border.

02:48.020 --> 02:49.110
Scouting.

02:49.430 --> 02:50.860
Scouting?

02:50.860 --> 02:52.240
It's the Demon Lord's Army.

02:52.240 --> 02:56.030
They were trying to cross
the river by building a bridge.

02:56.320 --> 02:58.070
Wait. Does that mean...?

02:58.070 --> 02:59.790
I destroyed their bridge,

02:59.790 --> 03:01.920
so we should be all right
for the time being.

03:02.370 --> 03:04.500
What part of that is scout—

03:05.960 --> 03:09.170
My head! It's going to explode!

03:09.670 --> 03:11.550
A fox beastman?

03:11.550 --> 03:13.090
Oh, her.

03:13.510 --> 03:14.920
You know her?

03:14.920 --> 03:17.430
Not personally...

03:17.800 --> 03:21.390
That girl appeared here
two years ago.

03:21.390 --> 03:22.890
She's only around 12.

03:22.890 --> 03:25.060
Yet, she made it here all by herself,

03:25.060 --> 03:27.350
evading all the bandits and kidnappers.

03:29.060 --> 03:30.270
Kidnappers?

03:30.270 --> 03:34.110
Demi-humans are extremely
valuable to them.

03:34.650 --> 03:37.700
Not only are they prized
for their physical appearance,

03:37.700 --> 03:41.280
some even have an aptitude
for rare magic.

03:42.450 --> 03:46.250
Does that include the ability
to show others strange visions?

03:46.250 --> 03:49.170
Visions? Like what?

03:49.830 --> 03:51.670
How should I put this...

03:52.040 --> 03:53.670
Like a nightmare.

03:53.670 --> 03:57.090
Like a future you hope
never comes to pass.

03:57.470 --> 03:59.390
Future, huh?

03:59.640 --> 04:04.560
There are supposedly beastmen who can
use a magic called precognition...

04:04.860 --> 04:06.020
Precognition?

04:06.020 --> 04:08.190
They're extremely rare.

04:08.190 --> 04:12.610
Even if such beastmen did exist, they'd be
well-guarded back in the Beastlands.

04:12.610 --> 04:13.900
What about it?

04:13.900 --> 04:17.820
O-Oh, it's nothing. I was just
reading about them in a book.

04:18.360 --> 04:19.220
Right...

04:20.320 --> 04:22.500
Beastmen who can see into the future...

04:22.990 --> 04:25.240
What if that girl was one of them?

04:26.330 --> 04:26.910
Huh?

04:28.190 --> 04:29.710
I'm going to see Lloyd-sama.

04:29.710 --> 04:31.710
You head back first.

04:32.080 --> 04:33.090
All right...

04:36.260 --> 04:38.260
That is all I have to report.

04:39.160 --> 04:40.220
I see.

04:40.220 --> 04:43.800
I apologize for putting you in danger.

04:43.800 --> 04:47.600
Thank you for halting their advance.

04:48.010 --> 04:48.940
It was nothing.

04:48.940 --> 04:52.690
But they should be
working on a new bridge.

04:52.690 --> 04:55.270
It will be completed in a few days.

04:55.270 --> 04:59.530
Indeed. And they will
begin their invasion.

05:04.120 --> 05:08.830
Tomorrow, we will inform the soldiers
and the citizens of the invasion.

05:08.830 --> 05:10.500
Sergio, begin the preparations.

05:10.890 --> 05:12.170
As you command.

05:12.540 --> 05:17.170
Siglis, I want to have a word with Suzune
and Kazuki before the night is up.

05:17.170 --> 05:18.300
Call them here at once.

05:18.300 --> 05:19.550
Right away.

05:21.340 --> 05:23.930
What do you think this
urgent matter's about?

05:24.190 --> 05:26.100
Well, it's probably...

05:26.100 --> 05:27.850
what else could it be?

05:28.520 --> 05:30.520
You think so?

05:34.810 --> 05:37.150
Hey, Celia. Good evening.

05:38.190 --> 05:40.030
Good evening, Suzune-sama.

05:40.740 --> 05:43.070
You, too, Kazuki-sama.

05:43.380 --> 05:45.070
E-Evening...

05:45.070 --> 05:47.330
Celia-san...

05:49.450 --> 05:51.330
My father is waiting.

05:51.330 --> 05:53.870
You may go see him now.

05:54.710 --> 05:57.630
Thanks! We'll see you later, then.

05:57.630 --> 05:58.710
Come, Kazuki-kun.

05:59.880 --> 06:00.690
Right...

06:05.300 --> 06:07.470
Did something happen
between the two of you?

06:07.470 --> 06:08.890
Wha...?

06:08.890 --> 06:10.550
No, nothing happened.

06:12.060 --> 06:13.640
Well, if you say so.

06:14.350 --> 06:16.230
All right, let's do this.

06:16.690 --> 06:17.360
Let's.

06:34.540 --> 06:35.710
I can't sleep

06:36.790 --> 06:39.190
Even if that was
a vision of the future,

06:39.750 --> 06:41.580
what can I do about it?

06:42.630 --> 06:46.510
That is why this is
a future you can change.

06:46.970 --> 06:51.600
Does that mean I can prevent it
from happening?

06:51.600 --> 06:55.060
She wants me to change the future?

06:55.060 --> 06:58.270
But there's no way I can do that...

07:01.720 --> 07:03.030
Huh? W-What is that?

07:03.530 --> 07:04.320
A ghost?

07:16.120 --> 07:17.540
Kazuki?

07:19.760 --> 07:22.130
I didn't expect to see you
at this time of night!

07:22.510 --> 07:23.300
My bad.

07:23.300 --> 07:25.800
You've got to get up
early to train, right?

07:25.800 --> 07:28.720
Nah, it's all right.

07:29.010 --> 07:32.560
You're in no position
to sleep in either, right?

07:32.560 --> 07:34.140
I mean, you're the great hero!

07:36.980 --> 07:38.220
Something wrong?

07:39.560 --> 07:42.590
Just now, we were called up by the king.

07:43.440 --> 07:44.900
And he told us...

07:44.900 --> 07:48.070
that the battle with
the Demon Lord's Army will soon begin.

07:48.870 --> 07:52.070
I was expecting it,
so I wasn't all too surprised.

07:53.240 --> 07:55.790
Senpai was already raring to go.

07:56.960 --> 07:58.270
As for me?

08:00.210 --> 08:01.170
As for me...

08:01.750 --> 08:04.380
when I pictured myself fighting,

08:04.380 --> 08:07.590
I couldn't fall asleep
and ran out of the castle.

08:07.590 --> 08:08.940
Now, here I am.

08:11.100 --> 08:14.010
I... ran away.

08:15.390 --> 08:17.640
Usato, I'm...

08:18.190 --> 08:19.400
scared...

08:20.270 --> 08:21.310
to fight.

08:23.070 --> 08:25.480
When I left the kingdom to train...

08:25.480 --> 08:27.330
When I fought monsters for real...

08:28.120 --> 08:29.530
I was really scared.

08:30.410 --> 08:33.490
My legs froze up
when I saw them for the first time.

08:33.490 --> 08:38.330
They put up a fierce resistance,
and when I finally managed to defeat them...

08:40.710 --> 08:43.250
I... realized.

08:43.250 --> 08:46.840
I realized just how lightly
I've been taking everything.

08:46.840 --> 08:50.050
The Demon Lord's Army will try to kill me
with everything they've got.

08:51.110 --> 08:53.140
I'm just so unbelievably scared.

08:55.410 --> 08:59.690
And yet... the people of this
kingdom are so kind to me.

08:59.690 --> 09:02.330
They support me and are counting on me.

09:03.310 --> 09:05.060
I can't stand it!

09:08.420 --> 09:09.580
Kazuki...

09:09.950 --> 09:11.740
you're a really cool guy, you know?

09:11.740 --> 09:12.740
What?

09:13.070 --> 09:18.160
I thought you always knew
what to do and never got scared.

09:18.570 --> 09:20.330
I mean, you're a cool guy, right?

09:20.330 --> 09:22.250
I get scared, too!

09:22.250 --> 09:23.110
Of course, you do.

09:23.660 --> 09:24.590
I know that now.

09:25.040 --> 09:30.380
The expectations of those
around you have been a burden.

09:30.740 --> 09:31.590
Usato.

09:32.410 --> 09:34.680
You don't have to, you know?

09:34.680 --> 09:37.470
You don't have to keep living up
to those expectations.

09:37.850 --> 09:41.500
Sometimes, it's all right
to put yourself first.

09:43.480 --> 09:45.720
Usato, what about you?

09:47.340 --> 09:49.860
Tell me what you really feel.

09:55.700 --> 09:57.530
I'm going.

09:58.410 --> 10:01.780
I'm going to save those who will fight
the Demon Lord's Army.

10:02.540 --> 10:04.330
Aren't you scared?

10:04.690 --> 10:06.500
Of course, I am.

10:07.460 --> 10:09.590
But that is what I decided.

10:10.290 --> 10:11.670
Decided?

10:11.670 --> 10:13.090
Are you serious?

10:13.090 --> 10:14.840
You could die!

10:15.260 --> 10:18.760
You were just dragged
into all this by accident!

10:19.680 --> 10:23.980
That might be how I got here...

10:25.060 --> 10:28.440
but I've experienced
many things since then.

10:30.650 --> 10:33.200
There were some tough times,

10:33.200 --> 10:35.820
but I've also met many people...

10:35.820 --> 10:40.330
people who accepted me
and showed me the way.

10:40.680 --> 10:42.910
I want to help them.

10:43.580 --> 10:44.490
Usato...

10:45.000 --> 10:47.630
That includes you, too.

10:48.590 --> 10:50.170
Obviously!

10:50.170 --> 10:53.300
It doesn't matter
if you fight or not.

10:53.300 --> 10:55.680
You're still my friend either way.

11:05.690 --> 11:08.270
I'm so lame!

11:09.000 --> 11:09.980
All right.

11:09.980 --> 11:13.440
I'm going to fight to protect
both you and Senpai.

11:14.650 --> 11:17.780
I don't know if I can fight as a hero,

11:17.780 --> 11:20.280
but I'll fight nonetheless!

11:20.280 --> 11:21.820
I want to help my friends...

11:21.820 --> 11:24.040
To help you!

11:24.040 --> 11:29.210
W-Wait! I know what I said,
but are you sure?

11:29.210 --> 11:33.510
I can't just sit here when you're
already resolved to fight, can I?

11:33.880 --> 11:35.590
I'll charge right ahead!

11:35.590 --> 11:39.600
Take my fear and fight...
in spite of it!

11:40.050 --> 11:41.930
Are you really sure?

11:42.560 --> 11:45.680
When I think about having
both you and Senpai by my side,

11:45.680 --> 11:47.940
I couldn't be more reassured!

11:48.300 --> 11:49.610
I'll be all right now!

11:50.360 --> 11:51.650
That's good to hear.

11:52.900 --> 11:54.070
Well then...

11:54.070 --> 11:55.650
let's do this together!

11:55.650 --> 11:56.990
Protect this kingdom...

11:56.990 --> 11:58.240
and everyone in it!

11:58.620 --> 11:59.410
Yeah,

11:59.410 --> 12:01.080
you got it!

12:02.740 --> 12:06.620
I-I just said something
really corny, didn't I?

12:07.670 --> 12:09.540
What are you talking about?

12:09.540 --> 12:12.460
I'm really glad I met you!

12:12.460 --> 12:13.520
Thanks for everything!

12:15.090 --> 12:18.340
Kazuki, you're way too cool
for your own good!

12:18.340 --> 12:20.180
No, you're the cool one!

12:22.890 --> 12:25.060
Good night, and thank you, Usato!

12:25.060 --> 12:26.720
Sure, any time!

12:32.270 --> 12:34.070
Time to hit the hay.

12:34.070 --> 12:37.190
I'll forget I ever said those corny lines.

12:37.190 --> 12:38.990
Yup. That's what I'll do.

12:38.990 --> 12:43.160
So, that's what you call bromance, huh?

12:43.160 --> 12:45.450
That was quite the show!

12:45.450 --> 12:47.910
I'm sorry, but I'm sleepy.

12:47.910 --> 12:50.920
Can we do this tomorrow, Inukami-senpai?

12:50.920 --> 12:53.670
Huh? That's all?

12:53.670 --> 12:57.380
Isn't this where you go...
"Oh! It's Suzu-tan! Why's she here?!"

12:57.380 --> 12:59.720
...or am I mistaken?

12:59.720 --> 13:03.100
When have I ever called you "Suzu-tan"?

13:03.870 --> 13:05.390
This is you we're talking about.

13:05.390 --> 13:08.020
I bet you noticed Kazuki acting weird.

13:08.230 --> 13:10.590
You then got worried
and followed him here.

13:11.940 --> 13:13.110
That's pretty much it.

13:13.110 --> 13:15.210
But there's nothing left for me to do.

13:15.610 --> 13:17.780
Looks like you've managed
to snap him out of it.

13:20.200 --> 13:24.660
To be honest, there's still a part of me
that doesn't want him to fight.

13:30.370 --> 13:33.630
Usato-kun, would you
rather I not fight?

13:34.590 --> 13:36.300
Of course.

13:36.300 --> 13:38.630
But your situation is different.

13:38.630 --> 13:42.770
You've already made up your mind
to live in this world.

13:44.640 --> 13:46.650
Yup. Guess you're right.

13:47.850 --> 13:49.520
Time for me to get back to the castle.

13:50.200 --> 13:52.830
It's going to be a big day tomorrow.

13:54.060 --> 13:55.110
Night!

13:55.770 --> 13:57.700
Thanks. Good night to you, too.

13:59.490 --> 14:03.610
I have a proclamation to make today!

14:04.070 --> 14:09.160
The Demon Lord's Army
has been sighted near the border.

14:09.160 --> 14:12.120
It is only a matter of time
before they invade.

14:12.960 --> 14:16.880
We plan to intercept them
in the grasslands.

14:17.290 --> 14:21.300
Two years ago, our troops successfully
repelled the Demon Lord's Army.

14:21.720 --> 14:25.470
Our enemy has undoubtedly
strengthened their forces.

14:26.010 --> 14:28.140
This time, it will not be as easy.

14:28.510 --> 14:29.720
However!

14:29.720 --> 14:32.310
We have also strengthened our forces.

14:32.850 --> 14:35.100
We have Hero Suzune and Hero Kazuki,

14:35.520 --> 14:38.320
two heroes summoned from another world

14:38.320 --> 14:40.400
who have pledged their powers to help us.

14:41.400 --> 14:45.450
We also have those from the Rescue Squad
who played a critical role two years ago!

14:45.860 --> 14:51.950
They are sure to do so once again with
their healing magic on the battlefield.

14:52.370 --> 14:55.870
I am sure some of you are worried.

14:56.380 --> 14:58.790
But... I am not!

14:59.250 --> 15:03.340
Our kingdom will emerge victorious!

15:04.420 --> 15:07.340
That is because...
I know our soldiers!

15:07.340 --> 15:11.970
They are brave, strong, and fearless.

15:11.970 --> 15:15.810
And they are standing right before me!

15:16.210 --> 15:18.020
Tomorrow, we fight!

15:18.020 --> 15:19.980
And we will...

15:19.980 --> 15:21.290
win!

15:36.710 --> 15:40.090
Celia-sama,
Hero Kazuki is here to see you.

15:45.800 --> 15:46.930
Kazuki-sama.

15:48.180 --> 15:49.600
I beg your pardon...

15:49.600 --> 15:50.680
for coming unannounced.

15:51.810 --> 15:54.270
No, I am glad.

15:56.980 --> 16:00.610
You're going, are you not?
Into battle?

16:00.940 --> 16:02.820
Yes, I am.
Together with everyone else.

16:02.820 --> 16:04.190
We depart tomorrow.

16:08.570 --> 16:12.240
I will pray for your success in battle.

16:13.080 --> 16:14.660
Thank you very much.

16:14.660 --> 16:17.620
I swear to protect this country
from the Demon Lord's Army.

16:22.500 --> 16:24.960
I'll be back... Celia.

16:28.010 --> 16:30.640
Good luck, Kazuki-sama.

16:31.350 --> 16:33.680
Please come back safe.

16:34.180 --> 16:34.810
I will.

16:46.190 --> 16:48.700
Wow! So cute!

16:48.700 --> 16:51.130
So, this is the Blurin
everyone's been talking about!

16:51.130 --> 16:52.450
Can I pet him?

16:52.450 --> 16:54.740
Fine by me.

16:54.740 --> 16:57.250
But I'm not sure
if he will let you.

16:57.500 --> 17:01.500
It's fine!
I'm sure we'll be fast friends!

17:03.250 --> 17:06.260
Sorry! He's not good with new people!

17:10.550 --> 17:12.760
Why?

17:12.760 --> 17:14.180
Kukuru-chan!

17:14.180 --> 17:15.930
Will you console me?

17:15.930 --> 17:16.930
Thank yo—

17:23.150 --> 17:25.270
Why?!

17:26.230 --> 17:27.859
O-Orga-san?!

17:27.859 --> 17:29.110
Are you all right?

17:29.900 --> 17:32.530
T-Thank you, Usato-kun.

17:32.930 --> 17:36.450
Sorry for the trouble we're causing you.

17:36.790 --> 17:38.000
Not at all.

17:38.000 --> 17:40.870
She's certainly a cheerful one.

17:41.250 --> 17:43.430
She's actually pretty nervous right now.

17:44.960 --> 17:48.720
Just like you,
it's her first time in battle.

17:49.240 --> 17:52.050
That's just her way of hiding her anxiety.

17:52.810 --> 17:54.510
I see...

17:54.510 --> 17:56.100
Hey, Usato!

17:56.100 --> 17:57.890
Big Sis wants to see ya in her room.

17:58.210 --> 18:00.640
Her room? The captain's quarters?

18:00.640 --> 18:02.810
Where else?

18:02.810 --> 18:08.570
I've never been called up
to her room before...

18:08.570 --> 18:11.820
What is she going to do to me?
Is it finally torture time?

18:12.740 --> 18:15.240
Hell if I know. Get movin'.

18:19.930 --> 18:22.120
May I come in? It's Usato.

18:22.580 --> 18:23.510
Enter!

18:32.170 --> 18:33.430
You were looking for me?

18:34.970 --> 18:37.510
We need to talk.

18:38.140 --> 18:42.850
Do you remember what your
role on the battlefield is?

18:43.230 --> 18:44.190
Let's see...

18:44.190 --> 18:48.770
to heal the injured together
with you on the front lines.

18:49.160 --> 18:50.360
That's right.

18:50.360 --> 18:52.780
But we will not do so at the beginning.

18:52.780 --> 18:56.570
Tong and the others will ferry
the wounded back to the rear.

18:56.570 --> 19:00.120
We'll treat them there together
with Orga and Ururu.

19:00.120 --> 19:01.950
Why won't we be going to the front lines?

19:02.310 --> 19:05.670
There's no point. There won't be many
wounded people at the start of battle.

19:05.670 --> 19:08.630
The front lines will be chaotic.
We'll be sitting ducks.

19:09.000 --> 19:09.990
You have a point...

19:10.570 --> 19:15.250
One more thing about
being on the front lines.

19:15.800 --> 19:18.140
Don't save the wrong people.

19:19.100 --> 19:21.600
Like not healing the enemy?

19:21.600 --> 19:23.560
Not that, you idiot.

19:23.990 --> 19:27.150
Don't go healing everyone you see.

19:28.480 --> 19:33.490
Let's say you see someone who's
still fighting despite being injured.

19:33.490 --> 19:35.570
What's gonna happen
if you try to heal him?

19:38.490 --> 19:40.530
I'll just be getting in his way.

19:40.530 --> 19:41.660
That's right.

19:41.660 --> 19:45.040
In battle, our troops will be
mixed with the enemy's.

19:45.040 --> 19:48.580
Use your judgment to decide
who to heal at a moment's notice.

19:49.580 --> 19:50.600
Understood!

19:55.420 --> 19:56.630
What's this?

19:57.050 --> 19:58.750
Look inside.

19:59.390 --> 20:00.220
Okay.

20:11.560 --> 20:13.400
The Rescue Squad uniform.

20:13.400 --> 20:16.570
It's made to help one
stand out on the battlefield.

20:16.990 --> 20:17.780
Right...

20:17.780 --> 20:19.990
It's yours, wear it!

20:22.870 --> 20:23.910
Right away!

20:27.660 --> 20:30.420
Gotta say, it fits you well.

20:30.420 --> 20:33.090
It was worth building up
all that muscle, huh?

20:33.090 --> 20:35.380
Y-You think?

20:35.380 --> 20:38.340
I certainly wouldn't have
looked good in it before—

20:41.390 --> 20:43.050
Listen here, Usato.

20:43.050 --> 20:45.680
Healers aren't immortal.

20:45.680 --> 20:48.020
Once you die, it's game over.

20:48.420 --> 20:49.690
Remember this!

20:49.690 --> 20:52.980
The one thing to never do
on the battlefield...

20:54.070 --> 20:57.150
is to take your life for granted.

20:57.470 --> 21:00.240
I... know that already.

21:00.240 --> 21:02.410
It's not like I want to die.

21:02.740 --> 21:04.330
- Are you an idiot?
- Ow!

21:06.990 --> 21:09.500
Talk is cheap.

21:09.500 --> 21:13.080
I know people who said
that crap and died anyway...

21:13.080 --> 21:16.250
and I know an idiot who's
just dying with regret.

21:17.670 --> 21:20.350
Don't underestimate
the value of your life.

21:20.350 --> 21:23.600
Being part of the Rescue Squad means
that you have to save yourself, too.

21:23.980 --> 21:27.100
Give me any of that
self-sacrificing crap...

21:27.100 --> 21:30.480
and I'll kill you before the enemy does.

21:34.730 --> 21:35.820
Very well.

21:35.820 --> 21:39.240
I will save everyone, including myself.

21:39.630 --> 21:41.780
Can you do that?

21:42.160 --> 21:44.910
You're the one who told me
to speak my ideals.

21:49.040 --> 21:52.210
Don't forget what you just said.

21:54.380 --> 21:55.050
Roger!

21:55.950 --> 21:56.950
Thank you, Captain!

22:04.640 --> 22:08.430
It doesn't matter if that was
a vision of the future or not.

22:08.800 --> 22:11.100
What I have to do is clear.

22:13.900 --> 22:16.310
Not let Kazuki or Senpai die.

22:16.310 --> 22:17.770
No matter what!
